%N A029909 Starting with each nonprime number (A018252), repeatedly sum prime factors (with multiplicity) until reaching 0 or a fixed point. Then a(n) is the fixed point (or 0).
%C A029909 Is this sequence generating all prime numbers greater than 3? Also how many times is each prime (greater than 3) generated in this sequence? - _Alexander R. Povolotsky_, Nov 05 2008
%C A029909 Records appear to correspond to A006512 (n>2). - _Bill McEachen_, Jun 10 2025
%H A029909 Paolo P. Lava, <a href="/A029909/b029909.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%e A029909 20 -> 2+2+5 = 9 -> 3+3 = 6 -> 2+3 = 5.
